---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="How We Cover Software · Contractor Software Hub"
  description="How CSH researches contractor software: official documentation, current pricing, linked user evidence, buying-fit analysis, and clear disclosure of hands-on testing."
  active="how"
>
  <section class="page-hero blueprint-bg">
    <div class="wrap-content">
      <div class="rule-label" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
        <span>Methodology</span>
        <span style="flex:1;"></span>
        <span>v3.2 · Updated Jul 2026</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="display hero-title">
        How we<br/>actually<br/><span class="accent">cover things.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="serif" style="font-size:clamp(18px, 2.2vw, 22px); line-height:1.45; color:var(--ink-2); max-width:820px; margin-top:24px;">
        Every review, comparison, and roundup on this site runs through the same pipeline. No exceptions for sponsors. No softening for affiliate partners. Most articles are source-researched from official product evidence and genuine user accounts; hands-on testing is claimed only when we actually performed it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="steps-section">
    <div class="wrap-content">
      <div class="steps-grid">
        {[
          { n: '01', h: 'Verify the product record', t: "We start with the vendor's current pricing, product pages, release notes, and support documentation. If pricing is hidden behind a demo, we say so. Load-bearing claims link to the exact source whenever one is publicly available." },
          { n: '02', h: 'Read the available user evidence', t: "We check relevant sources such as G2, Capterra, app stores, and trade forums. Some products have thousands of ratings; others have almost none. We report the sample honestly and never invent a score or imply that one complaint is a pattern." },
          { n: '03', h: 'Check contractor discussions', t: "Relevant Reddit communities and trade forums can expose workflow problems that do not appear in polished directories. We link the discussion, identify thin or conflicted samples, and separate firsthand experience from vendor, consultant, or competitor commentary." },
          { n: '04', h: 'Name the wrong buyer', t: "Every product has a contractor it's the wrong tool for. If we can't identify them, the research isn't complete. We call that out explicitly - \"not for\" is as important as \"right for\" in our coverage." },
          { n: '05', h: 'Verdict leads the piece', t: "Every review opens with a verdict - Top Pick, Recommended, Conditional, or Skip - plus a one-line summary. The body explains why. Scroll away if you want; the summary's already paid off." },
          { n: '06', h: 'Refresh on a tracked queue', t: "Pricing shifts and features ship. Timestamped freshness appears only when the article is attached to the quarterly review queue; the visible date and structured-data date come from the same field." },
        ].map(s => (
          <div class="step">
            <div class="step-n">{s.n}</div>
            <h2 class="display step-h">{s.h}</h2>
            <p class="serif step-t">{s.t}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ratings-explain">
    <div class="wrap-content">
      <div class="rule-label" style="color:var(--paper); margin-bottom:36px;">
        <span style="color:var(--orange);">What the ratings mean</span>
        <span style="flex:1;"></span>
        <span style="color:var(--graphite);">Four calls. No grade inflation.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ratings-grid">
        <div class="r-card top">
          <div class="r-stamp">TOP PICK</div>
          <p class="serif">We'd recommend this to a contractor we know, in the right profile, without hedging. Usually the strongest fit for a specific team size and trade.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="r-card rec">
          <div class="r-stamp">RECOMMENDED</div>
          <p class="serif">Solid. Well-built. Worth using - and in some cases worth preferring to a Top Pick if your profile tilts toward its strengths.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="r-card cond">
          <div class="r-stamp">CONDITIONAL</div>
          <p class="serif">Buy it only if you fit a narrow, specific profile. For everyone else, better options exist. We'll name the profile that makes it a fit.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="r-card skip">
          <div class="r-stamp">SKIP</div>
          <p class="serif">There's a better tool at the same price, or the product has a pattern of problems that outweigh its strengths. Rare but not hypothetical.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-pad">
    <div class="wrap-reading">
      <div class="rule-label" style="margin-bottom:28px;">
        <span>What source-researched means</span>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" style="margin-bottom:44px;">
        <p>A source-researched review is an editorial buying analysis built from official documentation, current public pricing, support material, and attributable user evidence. It is not a claim that CSH purchased, installed, or operated the software.</p>
        <p>When we complete hands-on testing, the article says what we tested, for how long, on which devices, and where the test stopped. Vendor or app-store screenshots are labeled as official product media; they are context, not proof of hands-on use.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rule-label" style="margin-bottom:28px;">
        <span>What we don't do</span>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <ul>
          <li>We don't rank tools by how much they pay in affiliate commissions.</li>
          <li>We don't inflate grades to keep vendors happy.</li>
          <li>We don't publish a "review" after a 15-minute demo.</li>
          <li>We don't imply hands-on testing when the article is source-researched.</li>
          <li>We don't recommend software you don't need yet.</li>
          <li>We don't lift copy from vendor pages.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>If you spot coverage that feels like it violates any of the above, email us. We'll look, we'll fix, and we'll credit the correction.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .accent { color: var(--orange); }
  .page-hero {
    padding: 64px 28px 48px;
    border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--ink);
    background-color: var(--paper);
  }
  .hero-title {
    font-size: clamp(56px, 9vw, 104px);
    line-height: 0.9;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .steps-section {
    padding: 72px 28px;
    border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .steps-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 56px 48px;
  }
  .step-n {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    color: var(--orange);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .step-h {
    font-size: clamp(24px, 3vw, 32px);
    line-height: 1;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  .step-t {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .ratings-explain {
    padding: 72px 28px;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
    border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .ratings-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
  }
  .r-card {
    padding: 28px;
    border: 1.5px solid currentColor;
    color: var(--orange);
  }
  .r-card.rec { color: var(--green); }
  .r-card.cond { color: #8fa6c6; }
  .r-card.skip { color: #d97c7c; }
  .r-stamp {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: 16px;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .r-card p {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--paper);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .section-pad {
    padding: 56px 28px;
    border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--ink);
  }
  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .steps-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 36px; }
    .ratings-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .page-hero, .steps-section, .ratings-explain, .section-pad { padding-left: 20px; padding-right: 20px; }
  }
</style>
